MyCompanyConfigurationWarning=Si prega di verificare le informazioni richieste per la propria azienda/organizzazione al fine di utilizzare le funzionalità di fatturazione elettronica. Queste informazioni sono necessarie per generare fatture elettroniche conformi e garantire la corretta sincronizzazione con l'Access Point.
ModifyCompanyInformation=Informazioni complete sull'azienda
EnableInvoiceExport=Abilita la generazione e l'esportazione delle fatture dei clienti
EnableInvoiceImport=Abilita l'importazione delle fatture di acquisto
EINVOICING_SYNC_TO_PA=Sincronizzazione delle fatture dei clienti (Dolibarr -> PA/PDP)
EINVOICING_AUTO_GENERATION=Sincronizzazione delle fatture di acquisto (Dolibarr <- PA/PDP)
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_IN_REAL_TIME=Generazione automatica della fattura elettronica al momento della convalida della fattura stessa.
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_CANCEL_IF_EINVOICE_FAILS=Annullare la registrazione della fattura se la generazione automatica della fattura elettronica non riesce.
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_CANCEL_IF_EINVOICE_FAILS2=Di default, la creazione della fattura viene effettuata anche se la generazione della fattura elettronica non riesce. In tal caso, è possibile rigenerare la fattura elettronica in un secondo momento.
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_GENERATION=Generazione automatica dei prodotti mancanti
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_GENERATION_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database, and if there is no default product to use on the supplier card, enabling this option will automatically create missing products during Access Point synchronization, otherwise the synchronization process is stopped until the product has been created manually or a default product for import is set on the vendor card.
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_BARCODE=Give a barcode to the products created at import
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_BARCODE_HELP=When a product is created from a received invoice, write the GTIN of the vendor (BT-157) as its barcode, or else take the next code of your barcode numbering module. Disabled by default: the created products get no barcode, so the codes of your numbering are kept for your own products. When your barcode setup requires a barcode on every product, the created products always get the next code of your numbering, whatever this option.
ErrorEInvoicingBarcodeRequiredOnImport=Your barcode setup requires a barcode on every product, and its numbering module gave none: create the product by hand, or set a mask in the barcode numbering module
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_ROUTING_MIXED=Default product type to use on import when not provided (Mixed invoices)
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_ROUTING_MIXED_HELP=A received invoice tells in its billing framework (BT-23) whether it bills goods (B), services (S) or both (M). Its lines with no matching product fall back on the default product of the vendor for B, on its default service for S. However, a mixed invoice does not say what is type of lines, so this option chooses the default type to use. As long as it is empty, the import of a mixed invoice stops with an error when one of its lines needs a type.
ErrorDefaultRoutingMixedUnset=This invoice bills both goods and services (billing framework BT-23 starting with M) without providing information on the type of line (product versus service). Choose in the setup of the module which type of item we must use (product vs service) when no type if provided by the seller.
SetDefaultRoutingMixed=Choose the type of item to use for mixed invoices
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_MATCH_CANONICAL_REF=Match vendor product references whatever their writing
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_MATCH_CANONICAL_REF_HELP=When a line of an incoming invoice carries a vendor product reference that no supplier price matches exactly, compare it again ignoring separators, case and accents, so that 'A1234-10_42' and 'A1234|10|42' are read as the same reference. This comparison is an approximation and can merge two references that differ only by their separators, so it is disabled by default. The exact comparison is always tried first. When several products of the supplier share the same simplified form, the line is left to the manual product mapping and a warning is written in the log.
EINVOICING_IMPORT_AS_FREE_LINES=Importa righe senza prodotto come righe di descrizione libere
EINVOICING_IMPORT_AS_FREE_LINES_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database, and if there is no default product to use on the supplier card, and automatic product creation is disabled, enabling this option will import the line as a free description line (using the XML label and description) without linking any product. If disabled, the synchronisation is stopped until the problem is resolved manually. Enabling this option is a VERY BAD IDEA!
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL=Use a catch-all product for lines with no product
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database and the supplier has no default product or service, the line is linked to the catch-all product chosen below, whatever the supplier. The default product or service of the supplier keeps priority. The lines it catches stay listed on the product mapping screen, so they can be reviewed. Not available with the automatic creation of products.
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_ID=Catch-all product
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_ID_HELP=Product linked to the lines of a received invoice for which no product and no default of the supplier was found. For example a generic "Miscellaneous purchases" product with its own purchase account.
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_LOCKED=Enable the option above to choose the product
