SupplierInvoiceComparisonVatBasisDifference=Differenza nell'importo della base IVA %s%% (fattura elettronica: %s / Fattura Dolibarr: %s)
SupplierInvoiceComparisonVatRateDifference=Differenza nell'importo dell'IVA %s%% (fattura elettronica: %s / Fattura Dolibarr: %s)
SupplierInvoiceComparisonVatRateNotFound=Aliquota IVA %s%% non trovata nella fattura Dolibarr
SupplierInvoiceComparisonSuggestVatCalculationMode=Ricalcola la fattura utilizzando la modalità %s per ottenere gli importi IVA corrispondenti alla fattura elettronica
EInvoiceImportVatModeRealigned=The invoice was recalculated using VAT calculation Mode %s to carry the totals of the received document, which announces a total VAT (BT-110) of %s and a total including VAT (BT-112) of %s, where the VAT calculation mode of this instance rebuilt a total of %s including VAT.
EInvoiceImportTotalsMismatch=The received document %s announces a total of %s including VAT (%s of VAT), while the invoice built from it totals %s including VAT. Neither VAT calculation mode rebuilds what the document announces, so the import could not reproduce it.
EInvoiceImportTotalsMismatchAction=That invoice cannot be validated, and no approval can be sent for it, until its totals are those of the document. The e-invoice file is attached to the invoice and readable from its XML preview: please report the problem with that file, both totals and your Dolibarr version.
EInvoiceImportPayableMismatch=The received document %s announces %s as the amount due for payment, while its own totals add up to %s (BR-CO-16: total with VAT, less what it says was already paid, plus its rounding amount). The two cannot both be right, so the invoice is held back rather than settled on a guess.
EInvoiceImportRoundingLineAdded=The received document rounds the amount due by %s. It is carried as a line of the invoice, so that the invoice totals what has to be paid.
EInvoiceLineFromVatBreakdown=Amount at the VAT rate of %s %% (the received document has no line)
EInvoiceNoLineNeedsDefaultProduct=This document has no line: only a default product of the vendor lets it be imported.
EInvoiceImportVatCarriedFromDocument=No VAT calculation mode rebuilds what the received document announces, so the invoice carries the amounts of the document itself: %s of VAT, %s including VAT. The difference was put on the last line of each rate, the taxable base of every rate being the announced one.
EInvoiceImportVatRoundedPerLine=The received document declares two VAT totals: %s rounded per line, which its totals add up to, and %s rounded per VAT rate in its breakdown. Its EXTENDED profile accepts both, and the invoice records the first one.
EInvoiceVatRoundedPerLineNote=The e-invoice this invoice was imported from declares two different VAT totals: %s rounded per line and %s rounded per VAT rate. Both are right, depending on where the rounding is made: per line, as accounting expects, or per VAT rate, as some e-invoicing rules do. Dolibarr imported the invoice with the first one.
EInvoiceTotalsMismatchBlocksValidation=This invoice does not total what the e-invoice it was imported from announces: the document says %s including VAT (%s of VAT), the invoice totals %s. Correct the invoice to the amounts of the document, or refuse the document to the vendor who issued it.
EInvoiceImportPrepaidMismatch=The received document %s announces %s including VAT as already paid, and the invoice built from it carries %s of deduction. Its totals are those of the document, but the deposit it deducts is not linked, so the invoice would be paid for the full amount.
EInvoiceImportPrepaidAlreadySettled=The received document %s announces %s including VAT as already paid, and the invoice built from it carries %s of deduction. Nothing in the document points at a deposit for the difference, so if that amount is really settled, record the payment on the invoice.
EInvoiceImportCreditNoteKeptAsReceived=The received credit note %s carries amounts with the sign the vendor gave them: a line it charges stays positive, as it is in the document, where Dolibarr would have made it a credit. Check the credit note against the document before validating it.
EInvoicePrepaidMismatchBlocksValidation=The e-invoice this invoice was imported from announces %s including VAT as already paid, and the invoice carries %s of deduction. Record the deposit invoice the vendor refers to and attach it as a discount, or refuse the document to the vendor who issued it.
EinvoicingCantDeleteADocumentLinkedToAnExistingSupplierInvoice=Il flusso %s non può essere eliminato perché è collegato alla fattura del fornitore Dolibarr n° %s
EinvoicingCantDeleteAValidatedSupplierInvoice=A supplier invoice created from a received e-invoice can no longer be deleted once it has been validated. Only its draft can, and deleting the draft leaves the received document itself in the flow list.
EinvoicingFailedToDetachTheFlowOfADeletedSupplierInvoice=Failed to detach the received e-invoice from the supplier invoice %s, so the invoice was not deleted.
EInvoiceReplacedSupplierInvoiceClosed=La fattura del fornitore sostituita da %s è stata chiusa come sostituita, quindi non può più essere pagata.
EinvoicingDuplicateDocumentForSupplierInvoice=Several e-invoicing documents were found for the supplier invoice %s. This should never happen and needs to be fixed in the database before this invoice can be validated or deleted.
EinvoicingCantDeleteATransmittedInvoice=Stai tentando di eliminare una fattura che è stata bloccata dopo essere stata trasmessa all'Access Point.
EInvoiceSupplierInvoiceLinkedToOrder=La fattura del fornitore è stata automaticamente collegata all'ordine di acquisto %s (corrispondente al riferimento dell'ordine BT-13).
EInvoiceSupplierOrderLinkAmbiguous=Diversi ordini di acquisto corrispondono al riferimento d'ordine %s per questo fornitore; la fattura non è stata collegata automaticamente. Si prega di collegarla manualmente.
EInvoiceSupplierOrderRefWrongSupplier=Esiste un ordine di acquisto con riferimento %s, ma appartiene a un fornitore diverso; la fattura non è stata collegata.
EInvoiceBuyerOrderReference=Riferimento dell'ordine dichiarato dal fornitore
EInvoiceReimport=Import E-invoice doc again
EInvoiceReimportRebuildConfirm=The document %s will be imported again from the access point into the draft supplier invoice it was imported into. Its lines and the files of the previous import are replaced; its reference, the files attached by hand, its events and its notes are kept. Nothing is sent to the access point.
EInvoiceReimportDone=The document %s has been imported again.
EInvoiceReimportFailed=The document %s could not be imported again.
EInvoiceReimportNotAReceivedInvoice=Only a received invoice can be imported again.
EInvoiceReimportNoFlowId=This record carries no flow identifier, so the access point cannot be asked for the document again.
EInvoiceReimportNoProvider=No access point is configured.
EInvoiceReimportInvoiceIsNotADraft=The supplier invoice %s is no longer a draft, so it cannot be imported again.
EInvoiceReimportOnlyOnADraft=A received e-invoice can only be imported again while the supplier invoice it created is still a draft.
EInvoiceReimportHint=A synchronization never imports again a flow that is already in this list. To import a received supplier invoice again - after deleting the draft it created, for example - open its flow, then use the "%s" action on the flow card.
EInvoiceBuyerOrderReferenceHelp=Il riferimento dell'ordine (BT-13) è riportato nella fattura elettronica ricevuta. Viene conservato così come inviato dal fornitore, indipendentemente dal fatto che corrisponda o meno a un ordine di acquisto di Dolibarr.
EInvoiceChorusBuyerSiretMissing=Chorus Pro support is on but the customer %s has no SIRET: rule BR-FR-CPRO-10 requires it as a buyer identifier (BT-46, scheme 0009) on a public sector invoice. Fill in the SIRET of the establishment being invoiced.
EInvoiceChorusBuyerSiretMalformed=The SIRET "%s" of the customer is not 14 digits: it was not sent as a buyer identifier (BT-46, scheme 0009), which rule BR-FR-CPRO-10 requires on a public sector invoice.
EInvoiceChorusSellerSiretMissing=Chorus Pro support is on but your company has no SIRET: rules BR-FR-CPRO-03 and BR-FR-CPRO-09 require it as a seller identifier (BT-29, scheme 0009) on a public sector invoice. Fill in the SIRET of your establishment in the company setup.
EInvoiceChorusSellerSiretMalformed=The SIRET "%s" of your company is not 14 digits: it was not sent as a seller identifier (BT-29, scheme 0009), which rules BR-FR-CPRO-03 and BR-FR-CPRO-09 require on a public sector invoice.
EInvoiceChorusReferenceTooLong=The %s reference is %s characters long, while rule BR-FR-CPRO-15 caps it at 50 for the public sector. It was sent as it is: "%s".
EInvoiceRoutingCodeRejected=Il codice di servizio Chorus Pro "%s" non è stato inviato come identificativo di instradamento dell'acquirente (BT-46, schema 0224): le regole BR-FR-24 e BR-FR-26 consentono solo lettere, cifre e i caratteri + - _ . fino a 100 caratteri. Si prega di correggerlo, altrimenti un acquirente pubblico che richiede un codice di servizio rifiuterà la fattura.
EInvoiceRoutingCodeNeedsExtendedProfile=Il codice di servizio Chorus Pro "%s" non è stato inviato come identificativo di instradamento dell'acquirente (BT-46, schema 0224): il profilo %s consente un singolo identificativo per l'acquirente. Selezionare il profilo EXTENDED-CTC-FR per inviarlo, come richiesto dalle regole BR-FR-CPRO-11 e BR-FR-CPRO-13 per un acquirente pubblico.
EInvoiceBuyerReference=Riferimento fattura acquirente
EInvoiceBuyerReferenceHelp=Riferimento di proprietà del cliente, utilizzato per instradare la fattura all'interno della propria organizzazione (unità aziendale, riferimento di servizio, casella di posta interna...). Inviato come BT-10. Il codice di servizio Chorus Pro non è presente in questo campo: viene inviato come identificativo dell'acquirente (BT-46).
WarningEinvoicingInvoiceStatusDifferentProvider=Fattura generata o inviata per un altro punto di accesso %s.
EinvoicingCantUnvalidateATransmittedInvoice=Stai tentando di modificare lo stato di una fattura che risulta bloccata dopo essere stata trasmessa all'Access Point.
EinvoicingCantModifyATransmittedInvoice=Stai tentando di modificare una proprietà che è bloccata dopo che la fattura è stata trasmessa al punto di accesso.
SendingStatus=Sending status
CheckingStatus=Checking status
CheckStatus=Check status

